invariant: INV-7
file: quic_initial.c
catches: quic_test
builds: bin/quic_test
reason: quic_initial_seal derives an Initial key for a version this
  build holds no salt or labels for and seals under version 1's, so a
  packet goes out under keys its version does not name.
  test/quic_initial_tests.h requires CH_EINVAL with nothing written for
  four such versions.

--- old
                      const uint8_t *pt, size_t pt_len, uint8_t *out, size_t cap, size_t *out_len) {
    if (!quic_version_derived(version)) {
        return CH_EINVAL;
    }
--- new
                      const uint8_t *pt, size_t pt_len, uint8_t *out, size_t cap, size_t *out_len) {
